{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Refreshable Braille Display.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Refreshable Braille Display.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"refreshable braille display refreshable braille display","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Refreshable Braille Display.md","fileName":"Refreshable Braille Display.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Refreshable Braille Display","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-28 03:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Tactile Communication and Sensory Substitution]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Tactile Communication and Sensory Substitution","Haptic Spatial Acuity","Braille Tactile Reading","haptics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Refreshable Braille Display.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Refreshable Braille Display.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"refreshable braille display refreshable braille display","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Refreshable Braille Display.md","fileName":"Refreshable Braille Display.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Refreshable Braille Display","heading":"Refreshable Braille Display","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A refreshable braille display uses individually controlled pins to raise the dot patterns for a changing line of digital text. After the reader finishes the displayed characters, the pins reconfigure to present the next segment from a computer or mobile device.\n\nThe actuator array must reproduce braille geometry within fingertip [[Haptic Spatial Acuity]] while fitting many cells into a compact, reliable device. Unlike speech output, it preserves spelling, punctuation, layout cues, and the active scanning process of [[Braille Tactile Reading]], but the number of simultaneously available characters is limited by physical size and cost.","tags":["baby"],